# Deploy target — DigitalOcean Docker host

Provisions the VM `deploy/compose.yaml` runs on: one Docker droplet
plus a firewall for SSH and the service port. State is remote in a
Spaces bucket (binding spec §5); one state per environment via
workspaces. Credentials ride the environment, never a file:

```sh
export DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN=…        # API token, read by both configs
export SPACES_ACCESS_KEY_ID=…      # Spaces key, for the bootstrap config
export SPACES_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=…
export AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID="$SPACES_ACCESS_KEY_ID"          # the same key,
export AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY="$SPACES_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY"  # for the S3 state backend
```

## Once per project

```sh
./bootstrap.sh    # provisions the state bucket, then `tofu init`
```

The bootstrap config keeps local state on purpose — the bucket is the
one resource that cannot live inside the remote state it hosts.
Commit `bootstrap/terraform.tfstate`; it contains no secrets.

## Per environment

```sh
tofu workspace new dev    # once per environment; `tofu workspace select` thereafter
tofu apply -var ssh_key_name=<your-uploaded-key>
```

## Deploying

The release pipeline pushes the image; the descriptor runs it here.
Config rides the environment of this one command — nothing is baked
into the host:

```sh
DOCKER_HOST="ssh://root@$(tofu output -raw ipv4)" \
  IMAGE=<registry>/<%= projectName %>:v1.2.3 \
  docker compose -f ../../deploy/compose.yaml up -d
```
